msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetAiTraffic.php:39
msgid "AI traffic: referrals and crawlers"
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetAiTraffic.php:46
msgid "Reports AI-related traffic in two separate blocks that must never be mixed: \"referrals\" (human visitors who arrived from an AI assistant like ChatGPT or Claude, including the referred pages, already part of the human view count) and \"crawlers\" (hits from AI crawlers like GPTBot or ClaudeBot, which never execute JavaScript and are only counted if AI-crawler tracking is enabled in the plugin settings)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetAiTraffic.php:118
msgid "Use it specifically for AI-related traffic. For a general referrer breakdown (search, social, direct, etc.) use get-dims-breakdown instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetAiTraffic.php:119
msgid "The crawlers block is only populated if AI-crawler tracking is enabled in the plugin settings — check ai_crawler_tracking_enabled in the response before presenting an empty list as \"no crawler traffic\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetContentTrends.php:38
msgid "Content view trends"
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetContentTrends.php:45
msgid "Returns views over time, bucketed by day, week or month, for specific posts or content types."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetContentTrends.php:120
msgid "Use it for a time series. For a single-point ranking or total, use list-most-viewed or get-views-summary instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetDimsBreakdown.php:40
msgid "Traffic breakdown by device or referrer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetDimsBreakdown.php:47
msgid "Breaks down site-wide traffic by device screen size (\"viewport\") or by where visitors came from (\"referrer\": direct, internal, search, social, ai assistants, other), aggregated per day, never per individual visit."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetDimsBreakdown.php:117
msgid "Use it for a site-wide breakdown of device size or referrer source. It is not per-post — for a single post use get-post-views."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetDimsBreakdown.php:118
msgid "Data only covers the period since this dimension started being recorded — see data_available_since in the response."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetPostViews.php:38
msgid "Post view stats"
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetPostViews.php:45
msgid "Returns the total views, first and last view, and the 90-day daily series for a specific post, identified by ID or URL."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetPostViews.php:85
msgid "Provide post_id or url to identify the post."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetPostViews.php:94
msgid "No published post was found with that ID or URL."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetPostViews.php:129
msgid "Use it for a specific post. For a ranking or a site-wide summary, use list-most-viewed or get-views-summary."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetViewsSummary.php:38
msgid "Site views summary"
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetViewsSummary.php:45
msgid "Returns site-wide totals: accumulated views, how many posts have traffic and how many don't, for a given set of content types."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/GetViewsSummary.php:102
msgid "Use it for site-wide aggregated totals, not for a ranking. For a ranking use list-most-viewed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListMomentum.php:39
msgid "Rising and falling content"
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListMomentum.php:46
msgid "Compares the last N days of views against the equal-length period right before them, and returns which posts are gaining or losing views."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListMomentum.php:109
msgid "Use it for a ranking of change between two periods. For a single-period ranking use list-most-viewed, and for a time series use get-content-trends."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListMostViewed.php:39
msgid "Most viewed content"
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListMostViewed.php:46
msgid "Returns the posts with the most views, optionally narrowed to a date window and to specific content types."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListMostViewed.php:123
msgid "Use it when asked for a ranking by view count. If instead they ask for content without recent views, use list-stale-content."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListMostViewed.php:124
msgid "With no date window, returns the exact all-time total. With a window, the data only covers the period since the daily aggregate was installed — see data_available_since in the response."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListStaleContent.php:38
msgid "Content without recent views"
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListStaleContent.php:45
msgid "Returns published posts that have never been viewed, or that have not been viewed in a while. Explicitly includes content that has never had a single view."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListStaleContent.php:115
msgid "Use it when asked for content with no recent traffic, or never viewed. If instead they ask for a ranking by views, use list-most-viewed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Mcp/Tools/ListStaleContent.php:116
msgid "Includes content that has never had a single view (null last_viewed_at), not just content that stopped being viewed."
msgstr ""

